{%- comment -%}
  theinmag-editorial-card
  Renders one card for theinmag-blog-index-editorial. Variant decides
  the markup shape:
    feature       - full-width photo with white text overlay
    large_left    - image-on-top, dark text below on lavender bg
    right_small   - same as large_left, smaller, divider above
    bottom_small  - same as large_left, smaller, two-up row

  Inputs (one of these must be set):
    block    - section block with curated settings (legacy path)
    article  - Article object (auto-pull or block-with-article path)
    variant  - one of feature|large_left|right_small|bottom_small

  Data-source priority (locked 2026-05-18):
    1. If `article` is set directly via render param → article data wins
    2. Else if `block.settings.article` is set → article data wins
    3. Else fall back to block.settings.* overrides (placeholder pattern)

  This is a DELIBERATE flip from the earlier override-wins behaviour.
  Once you pick an Article in the block, you get the article's real
  title / excerpt / image / link / topic / audience automatically -
  no need to also clear the override fields one by one.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign variant = variant | default: 'large_left'
  assign extra_class = extra_class | default: ''

  comment
  Resolve article source. Direct param wins (auto-pull path), else
  block.settings.article (curated-with-article path).
  endcomment
  if article == blank and block != blank
    assign article = block.settings.article
  endif

  comment
  ARTICLE PATH: when article is set, article data wins for everything.
  endcomment
  if article != blank
    assign title = article.title

    capture excerpt
      render 'theinmag-card-excerpt', article: article, words: 20
    endcapture
    assign excerpt = excerpt | strip

    assign topic = article.metafields.field_notes.primary_topic
    if topic == blank
      assign topic = article.tags.first
    endif

    assign card_link = article.url

    assign image_src = ''
    if article.image != blank
      assign image_src = article.image | image_url: width: 1600
    endif

    assign image_alt = article.image.alt | default: article.title

    comment
    Map the article's read_audience metafield (kids/parents/mixed,
    blank = mixed) onto the toggle's vocabulary (all/kids/adults):
    kids -> kids, parents (legacy 'adults') -> adults, mixed/blank ->
    all. 'all' shows on every toggle; 'kids' and 'adults' each show
    only on their own toggle (plus 'all'). Pre-2026-05-22 this
    collapsed parents into 'all', which let parent posts leak into
    the kids filter.
    endcomment
    assign read_aud = article.metafields.field_notes.read_audience | downcase
    if read_aud == 'kids'
      assign audience = 'kids'
    elsif read_aud == 'parents' or read_aud == 'adults'
      assign audience = 'adults'
    else
      assign audience = 'all'
    endif
  else
    comment
    OVERRIDE PATH: no article picked, use block.settings.* overrides
    (placeholder/legacy pattern). All lookups guarded so the snippet
    doesn't blow up if block is also nil (renders nothing in that
    edge case).
    endcomment
    assign title = ''
    assign excerpt = ''
    assign topic = ''
    assign card_link = ''
    assign image_src = ''
    assign image_alt = ''
    assign audience = 'all'

    if block != blank
      assign title = block.settings.title_override
      assign excerpt = block.settings.excerpt_override
      assign topic = block.settings.topic
      assign card_link = block.settings.link_override

      if block.settings.image != blank
        assign image_src = block.settings.image | image_url: width: 1600
      elsif block.settings.fallback_filename != blank
        assign image_src = block.settings.fallback_filename | asset_url
      endif

      assign image_alt = block.settings.image_alt | default: title
      assign audience = block.settings.audience | default: 'all'
    endif
  endif

  comment
    Real Kids Voices covers are the kid's own artwork (e.g. Mr. Bongo's
    giraffe). Anchor those covers to the top so the top of the piece -
    often the subject's head - stays in frame instead of being cropped
    by object-fit: cover. Keyed on the kid_first_name metafield, the same
    signal the article template uses for kid mode.
  endcomment
  assign is_kid_art = false
  if article != blank and article.metafields.field_notes.kid_first_name != blank
    assign is_kid_art = true
  endif

  assign card_class = 'theinmag-editorial__card theinmag-editorial__card--' | append: variant
  if extra_class != blank
    assign card_class = card_class | append: ' ' | append: extra_class
  endif

  assign shopify_attrs = ''
  if block != blank
    assign shopify_attrs = block.shopify_attributes
  endif
-%}

{%- capture card_inner -%}
  <span class="theinmag-editorial__card-cover">
    {%- if image_src != blank -%}
      <img
        class="theinmag-editorial__card-image{% if is_kid_art %} theinmag-editorial__card-image--top{% endif %}"
        src="{{ image_src }}"
        alt="{{ image_alt | escape }}"
        loading="lazy"
        width="1600"
        height="1000"
      >
    {%- else -%}
      <span class="theinmag-editorial__card-placeholder" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if variant == 'feature' -%}
      <span class="theinmag-editorial__card-scrim" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="theinmag-editorial__card-overlay">
        {%- if topic != blank -%}
          <span class="theinmag-editorial__card-topic theinmag-editorial__card-topic--on-photo">{{ topic }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if title != blank -%}
          <span class="theinmag-editorial__card-title theinmag-editorial__card-title--on-photo">{{ title }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if excerpt != blank -%}
          <span class="theinmag-editorial__card-excerpt theinmag-editorial__card-excerpt--on-photo">{{ excerpt }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </span>

  {%- if variant != 'feature' -%}
    <span class="theinmag-editorial__card-body">
      {%- if topic != blank -%}
        <span class="theinmag-editorial__card-topic">{{ topic }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if title != blank -%}
        <span class="theinmag-editorial__card-title">{{ title }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if excerpt != blank -%}
        <span class="theinmag-editorial__card-excerpt">{{ excerpt }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- if card_link != blank -%}
  <a class="{{ card_class }}" href="{{ card_link }}" data-audience="{{ audience }}" {{ shopify_attrs }}>{{ card_inner }}</a>
{%- else -%}
  <div class="{{ card_class }}" data-audience="{{ audience }}" {{ shopify_attrs }}>{{ card_inner }}</div>
{%- endif -%}
